# Prior art. The divisibility criterion implemented here is Pascal's; these are
# the works that contain the mathematics this repository rediscovered and
# implements. If you are citing the mathematics rather than this implementation,
# cite these instead. The claim-by-claim mapping is in the README's Prior Art
# section.
references:
  - type: generic
    title: >-
      De numeris multiplicibus ex sola characterum numericorum additione
      agnoscendis
    authors:
      - family-names: Pascal
        given-names: Blaise
    year: 1665
    notes: >-
      Written c. 1654, presented to the Academie Parisienne in 1654, published
      1665 in Traite du triangle arithmetique. The general divisibility
      criterion: replace each power of ten by its remainder modulo the divisor.
      This is the rule implemented by this repository.
  - type: article
    title: "Note sur la divisibilite des nombres"
    authors:
      - family-names: Zbikowski
        given-names: A.
    journal: >-
      Bulletin de l'Academie imperiale des sciences de St. Petersbourg, Classe
      physico-mathematique
    volume: 3
    start: 151
    end: 153
    year: 1861
    notes: >-
      The family of trimming tests to which the 1997 equation of this project
      belongs.
  - type: article
    title: "Zbikowski's Divisibility Criterion"
    authors:
      - family-names: Cherniavsky
        given-names: Yonah
      - family-names: Mouftakhov
        given-names: Artour
    journal: The College Mathematics Journal
    volume: 45
    issue: 1
    start: 17
    end: 21
    year: 2014
    doi: 10.4169/college.math.j.45.1.017
  - type: article
    title: "Divisibility Tests"
    authors:
      - family-names: Khare
        given-names: Apoorva
    journal: >-
      Furman University Electronic Journal of Undergraduate Mathematics
    volume: 3
    start: 1
    end: 5
    year: 1997
    url: "https://scholarexchange.furman.edu/fuejum/vol3/iss1/1/"
    notes: The summing tests with inverse-of-10 weights.
  - type: article
    title: "Divisibility tests with weighted digital sums"
    authors:
      - family-names: Pal
        given-names: Palash B.
    year: 2005
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0507011"
    notes: >-
      arXiv:math/0507011. Horner-form test for divisors ending in 1, 3, 7, 9,
      with proof; notes explicitly that it does not yield the remainder.
  - type: article
    title: "General Divisibility Criteria"
    authors:
      - family-names: Grinberg
        given-names: Anatoly A.
      - family-names: Luryi
        given-names: Serge
    year: 2014
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.5486"
    notes: >-
      arXiv:1401.5486. The two-parameter universal criterion for any divisor in
      any base. The 1997 equation of this project is exactly their restricted
      rule for the parameter choice q = CEIL(10/b2) - 1.
  - type: article
    title: "Divisibility Tests: A History and User's Guide"
    authors:
      - family-names: McDowell
        given-names: Eric L.
    journal: MAA Convergence
    year: 2018
    url: >-
      https://old.maa.org/press/periodicals/convergence/divisibility-tests-a-history-and-users-guide
    notes: >-
      History of the field, with dedicated sections on the Pascal and Zbikowski
      tests.
  - type: article
    title: "Divisibility Tests Unified: Stacking the Trimmings for Sums"
    authors:
      - family-names: O'Shea
        given-names: Edwin
    journal: Mathematics Magazine
    year: 2019
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.04903"
    notes: >-
      arXiv:1903.04903. Proves that the trimming and summing families of tests
      are the same tests, in both directions.
  - type: article
    title: "Divisibility Tests, Old and New"
    authors:
      - family-names: Ganzell
        given-names: Sandy
    journal: The College Mathematics Journal
    volume: 48
    issue: 1
    start: 36
    end: 40
    year: 2017
    doi: 10.4169/college.math.j.48.1.36
  - type: book
    title: "Vedic Mathematics"
    authors:
      - family-names: Tirthaji
        given-names: Bharati Krishna
    publisher:
      name: Motilal Banarsidass
    year: 1965
    notes: >-
      The osculator (Ekadhikena Purvena) construction, which produces the same
      multipliers as Zbikowski's test.
  - type: book
    title: "The Moscow Puzzles: 359 Mathematical Recreations"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kordemsky
        given-names: Boris A.
    editors:
      - family-names: Gardner
        given-names: Martin
    publisher:
      name: Dover Publications
    year: 1992
    notes: Problem 320 -- the times-five walk for testing divisibility by 7.
  - type: book
    title: >-
      History of the Theory of Numbers, Volume I: Divisibility and Primality
    authors:
      - family-names: Dickson
        given-names: Leonard Eugene
    publisher:
      name: Dover Publications
    year: 2005
